 ("Services", "ApiCalls", "ServiceEndpoint", "https://api.openweathermap.org/geo/1.0/direct",
  "An API is the way one program is asked for data by another, and an endpoint is the URL at which one request is answered; services put a version number into it, such as /geo/1.0/ and /data/2.5/, so that an old version can be retired.",
  (X("city_name = 'San Francisco'; state_code = 'CA'; country_code = 'US'; API_key = '30ee784a80d81480dab1749d33980112'\nurl = f'https://api.openweathermap.org/geo/1.0/direct?q={city_name},{state_code},{country_code}&appid={API_key}'\nimport urllib.parse\nout = (url, urllib.parse.urlsplit(url).path)"), "('https://api.openweathermap.org/geo/1.0/direct?q=San Francisco,CA,US&appid=30ee784a80d81480dab1749d33980112', '/geo/1.0/direct')")),
